# THROWN — right-click to hurl it, and it goes off WHERE IT LANDS.
#
# Two components ride on the stack and they are a pair:
#   WishThrowTag     makes the right-click throw a snowball carrying this feature's tag, which is
#                    what the trail clock below watches;
#   WishHitFunction  runs act() AT the impact point, AS the thrower.
#
# The landing was solved once in the mod (commit a18b5e0) precisely so no wish has to trail marker
# entities by hand — so there is no per-tick "where did it get to" bookkeeping here, and none should
# be added.
#
# The trail is not decoration. A thrown thing that is invisible in flight reads as the click having
# done nothing at all, which is the same complaint as an ability with no telegraph.
import common

function give()
${GIVES}
    /tellraw @s {"text":"${GIVE_MESSAGE}","color":"${HEX}"}
end

function act()
    /function $namespace:effect
end

clock tick
    /execute as @e[type=minecraft:snowball,tag=${FEATURE}_fly] at @s run particle ${TRAIL} ~ ~ ~ 0.05 0.05 0.05 0.01 3 force
end

${EFFECT_BLOCK}
